    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Beautiful two bedroom residence located in a quiet cul de sac in Woodleigh. No. 22 extends to c. 74.32 sq. mts and has been lovingly cared for  and  is presented in excellent condition. On entering you are greeted by a small hallway which leads to a bright spacious living room overlooking the front garden. It has a feature fireplace with gas fire inset and wooden flooring. There is under-stairs storage also. To the back of the house lies the ,kitchen dining room with modern kitchen with tiled floor and splashback and sliding patio doors to rear garden. Upstairs there are two double bedrooms with plenty of light. Both bedrooms have fitted wardrobes. The bathroom has been remodeled and now includes a corner shower cubicle, sink with vanity unit and marble effect tiling on walls and floors. Outside there is communal parking in front of the house and a cottage style front garden. The rear garden has a small lawned area and low maintenance stone patio area with barna shed. This is a lovely family home perfect for those looking to downsize, first time buyers or investors alike. \r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\nThis home is perfectly located overlooking a large green area with mature trees to the front of the property, in the popular Woodleigh development on the Dublin side of Blessington Village. All amenities – shops, churches, schools, pubs and restaurants – are within walking distance while the Town Centre development, which includes Dunnes Stores, the library and various other retail and leisure outlets are on your doorstep. Blessington is a popular commuter's choice being only 18 miles from the city and also with the benefit of a regular Dublin Bus service (No 65).\r\nNaas: c. 8 miles. Tallaght: 10 Miles. Dublin City Centre: c. 18 miles.\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE/ FEATURES:\r\nCommunal parking to front.\r\nSmall front garden.\r\nGenerous rear garden.\r\nUpgraded kitchen & bathroom.\r\nGas fired central heating."
      },
      {
